{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Game Verb.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Game Verb.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"game verb game verb","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Game Verb.md","fileName":"Game Verb.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Game Verb","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 15:28\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Game Mechanics and Rules]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Mechanics and Rules","Game Rule","Game-Player System","Game Part","Meaningful Decision","agamedesignvocabulary.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Game Verb.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Game Verb.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"game verb game verb","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Game Verb.md","fileName":"Game Verb.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Game Verb","heading":"Game Verb","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A game verb is a [[Game Rule]] that gives the player liberty to act within the game. It is a rule through which the player can change the system, such as moving, jumping, firing, rotating, or placing a piece.\n\nVerbs are the player's side of the [[Game-Player System|game-player dialogue]]. They let the player test other rules, learn how [[Game Part|game objects]] behave, and make [[Meaningful Decision|meaningful decisions]]. A focused set of verbs gives a design a clearer interactive vocabulary.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Mechanics and Rules","Game Rule","Game-Player System","Game Part","Meaningful Decision","agamedesignvocabulary.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Game Verb.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Game Verb.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"game verb game verb","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Game Verb.md","fileName":"Game Verb.